{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BKmyvD5aYNt8UGVbwZGTog","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0513_3/projects/symb_invariant_consensus/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Writing Plan — symb_invariant_consensus\\\\n# Generated: 2026-05-17T17:00:00Z\\\\n# Updated: 2026-05-17 — Oracle result (exp-021) incorporated, narrative upgraded\\\\n# Paper Agent Step 1 output\\\\n\\\\nmeta:\\\\n  venue: EMNLP 2026\\\\n  track: main\\\\n  template: templates/latex/acl/\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"ACL template shared by EMNLP; confirm 2026 style options when official EMNLP 2026 CFP releases\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8\\\\n  deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    LLM self-extracted FOL constraints cannot improve majority voting (SICA = SC across\\\\n    5 models x 3 domains, N>1,300), but this is NOT a failure of the aggregation mechanism:\\\\n    Oracle-SICA with gold FOL + Z3 achieves +8.82pp (p<0.001), proving MAX-SAT aggregation\\\\n    is effective given high-quality constraints. The sole bottleneck is LLM self-extraction\\\\n    quality. We provide a complete diagnosis: (1) characterize the capability trap,\\\\n    (2) localize the failure to extraction (not aggregation), (3) quantify the recoverable\\\\n    performance gap (+8.82pp).\\\\n  paper_type: \\\\\\\"Diagnostic analysis paper (negative result + causal localization + constructive upper bound)\\\\\\\"\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-17T17:00:00Z\\\\n\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 220\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: symbolic methods propose extracting FOL constraints from LLM traces to improve aggregation, but same-model self-extraction has not been rigorously evaluated\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Method: systematic evaluation of SICA (MAX-SAT over self-extracted FOL) across 3 domains x 5 model families (N>1,300)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Negative result: SICA provides no gain over SC in all conditions (all delta n.s.)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Causal localization: Oracle-SICA (gold FOL + Z3) achieves +8.82pp (p<0.001), proving aggregation works but self-extraction is the bottleneck\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Constructive: temperature ablation confirms diversity is not the issue; trained extractors / external provers can unlock +8.82pp\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1300\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: neuro-symbolic methods (Logic-LM, DyLoS, Aristotle, FoVer) show promise augmenting LLM reasoning with formal solvers\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: these methods use trained verifiers or external solvers; does same-model self-extraction suffice?\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Our approach: systematic SICA evaluation + oracle control experiment to separate extraction from aggregation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Key finding: aggregation mechanism is sound (+8.82pp with gold constraints), but self-extraction produces non-discriminative constraints\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Positioning: DyLoS/Aristotle/FoVer succeed because they avoid same-model self-extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: [C1] capability trap characterization, [C2] causal localization via oracle experiment, [C3] quantified recoverable gap (+8.82pp), [C4] C0 diagnostic\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n    figures: [fig1_pipeline]\\\\n    citation_hints:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Logic-LM, LINC, DyLoS, Aristotle, FoVer for neuro-symbolic context\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Wang et al. 2023 SC, Chen et al. 2023 USC for baselines\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 900\\\\n    phase: 1\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 1: SC and extensions (SC, USC, weighted SC, scaling)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 2: Neuro-symbolic reasoning (Logic-LM, LINC, DyLoS, Aristotle, FoVer, LogicAgent) — distinguish trained/external verifiers from same-model self-extraction\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 3: Test-time compute and reasoning models (Snell et al., DeepSeek-R1, diversity-aware TTS)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 4: Verification and reranking (ORM, PRM, Math-Shepherd)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 5: Constraint satisfaction in NLP (SATBench, LLM+CP)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Cluster 6: Debate and multi-agent aggregation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    word_budget: 1400\\\\n    phase: 1\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"SICA pipeline: K-trace generation -> FOL constraint extraction -> deduplication -> weighted partial MAX-SAT -> answer selection\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"MAX-SAT formulation with EXPLICIT cross-answer evaluation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"C0 definition: multi-candidate rate as necessary-but-insufficient condition\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle experiment design: replace self-extracted constraints with FOLIO gold FOL annotations; Z3 satisfiability check as constraint verification\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Scope statement: same-model self-extraction pipeline; oracle as causal intervention\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    figures: [fig1_pipeline]\\\\n    notation_table:\\\\n      K: \\\\\\\"number of reasoning traces sampled per problem\\\\\\\"\\\\n      T: \\\\\\\"temperature for trace generation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      C: \\\\\\\"set of extracted FOL constraints\\\\\\\"\\\\n      c_i: \\\\\\\"individual constraint from trace t_i\\\\\\\"\\\\n      w_i: \\\\\\\"weight of constraint c_i\\\\\\\"\\\\n      A: \\\\\\\"candidate answer set {a_1, ..., a_m}\\\\\\\"\\\\n      C0: \\\\\\\"multi-candidate rate: fraction of problems with |A|>1\\\\\\\"\\\\n    registry_refs: [sica_expanded_14b, sica_constraint_ablation_013, exp-021-oracle-folio]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    word_budget: 2400\\\\n    phase: 1\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Setup: 5 models x 3+ domains, K=12, T=0.7\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Models: Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct, Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.3, LLaMA-3.1-8B-Instruct, DeepSeek-R1-Distill-Qwen-7B, QwQ-32B\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Datasets: FOLIO (formal logic, 204), ProofWriter (deductive, 600), StrategyQA (commonsense, 200), ARC-Challenge (science, 60), GSM8K (math, 30 pilot)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Metrics: accuracy, C0, McNemar test, bootstrap CI\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Main results (T1): SICA = SC all conditions, N>1,300\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle control (T2): Oracle-SICA 88.24% vs SC 79.41% vs SICA(self) 79.41%, +8.82pp, p=6.15e-05\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Constraint ablation (T3): MAX-SAT = count-only = random-weight (n=804) [BLOCKED: exp-013 data pending, leave placeholder]\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Temperature ablation (T4): report 3 points only (T=0.3/0.5/1.0 from same ablation run, C0 30%->38.3%->43.3%); T=0.7 C0=53.3% from sica_d012_14b is a different run, note in table footnote; OR wait for T=0.7 re-run\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Two failure regimes: (1) Constraint-present but non-discriminative (FOLIO/PW, C0>20%, extraction >80% but precision ~50%) = capability trap core; (2) Constraint-absent / extraction-degenerate (GSM8K extraction 14.7%, ARC C0<5%) = SICA has no operational basis\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Operating regime: QwQ C0<5% -> SICA=SC; instruction models C0=38-62% -> constraints non-discriminative; GSM8K illustrates C0-degenerate regime (do NOT use to argue non-discriminative constraints)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    registry_refs:\\\\n      - sica_expanded_14b\\\\n      - exp-010-mistral-v3\\\\n      - exp-014-deepseek-r1-7b\\\\n      - exp-019-llama8b-strategyqa-200\\\\n      - exp-020-llama8b-folio-204\\\\n      - sica_constraint_ablation_013\\\\n      - exp-021-oracle-folio\\\\n      - temperature-ablation-t03\\\\n      - temperature-ablation-t05\\\\n      - temperature-ablation-t10\\\\n      - exp-005\\\\n      - exp-009-overhead-analysis\\\\n      - exp-016-weighted-sc\\\\n      - sica_k_sensitivity_14b\\\\n      - exp-017-strategyqa-v3\\\\n      - exp-018-arc-v2\\\\n      - exp-012-gsm8k-pilot\\\\n    tables: [tab1_main_results, tab2_oracle_control, tab3_ablation, tab4_temperature]\\\\n    figures: [fig2_capability_scatter, fig3_operating_regime]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: discussion\\\\n    word_budget: 600\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Oracle experiment as causal intervention: isolates extraction from aggregation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Why DyLoS/Aristotle/FoVer work: they bypass same-model self-extraction (trained verifiers, external provers, multi-paradigm solvers)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Constructive direction: better extraction methods (trained verifiers, external provers) can unlock +8.82pp potential\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"C0 as deployment diagnostic: necessary but not sufficient\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Limitations: FOLIO-only oracle (gold FOL available), n=60 for some conditions, no trained extractor comparison\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    word_budget: 350\\\\n    phase: 2\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Summary: SICA provides no accuracy gain over SC across 5 models and 3 domains\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"But aggregation mechanism is sound: +8.82pp with gold constraints (p<0.001)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Sole bottleneck: LLM self-extraction quality (non-discriminative constraints)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Practical: C0 as zero-cost go/no-go diagnostic\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Future: trained extractors, external provers, cross-model constraints as paths to unlock potential\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_pipeline\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      SICA pipeline diagram: K reasoning traces (with temperature sampling) ->\\\\n      FOL constraint extraction -> deduplication -> weighted partial MAX-SAT solver ->\\\\n      answer selection. Side-by-side with SC (majority voting) for comparison.\\\\n      Must show where cross-answer evaluation happens. Add oracle branch showing\\\\n      gold FOL + Z3 replacing self-extraction.\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:6\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig2_capability_scatter\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Hero figure: per-problem analysis of n=307 multi-candidate problems from exp-001.\\\\n      Scatter of vote_entropy vs constraint_exclusion_rate, colored by SICA flip direction\\\\n      (positive flip / negative flip / no change). Shows constraints are non-discriminative\\\\n      regardless of diversity level.\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"artifact: f2_per_problem_csv (art_20260517_c29c72)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig3_operating_regime\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: >\\\\n      Operating regime summary: grouped bar or heatmap showing C0, SICA-SC delta,\\\\n      and constraint quality across all model-domain conditions. Include oracle result\\\\n      as highlighted row/bar showing the gap between self-extraction and gold constraints.\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: sica_expanded_14b, exp-010-mistral-v3, exp-014-deepseek-r1-7b, exp-019-llama8b-strategyqa-200, exp-020-llama8b-folio-204, exp-005, exp-021-oracle-folio\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n  - table_id: tab1_main_results\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Main results: SICA vs. SC accuracy across 5 model families and 3 reasoning domains. No condition shows statistically significant improvement (N>1,300 combined).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Model, Domain, N, \\\\\\\"SC(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SICA(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Delta(pp)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"p\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: sica_expanded_14b, exp-010-mistral-v3, exp-014-deepseek-r1-7b, exp-019-llama8b-strategyqa-200, exp-020-llama8b-folio-204, exp-005, exp-017-strategyqa-v3, exp-018-arc-v2\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"n=60 conditions marked with dagger; 'suggestive/consistent with' language per D037\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab2_oracle_control\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Oracle control experiment on FOLIO (N=204): replacing self-extracted constraints with gold FOL annotations + Z3 verification yields +8.82pp over SC (p<0.001), proving aggregation mechanism is effective.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Method, \\\\\\\"Constraint Source\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Accuracy(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Delta vs SC(pp)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"McNemar p\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-021-oracle-folio\\\\\\\"\\\\n    rows:\\\\n      - [\\\\\\\"SC (majority vote)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"N/A\\\\\\\", 79.41, \\\\\\\"—\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"—\\\\\\\"]\\\\n      - [\\\\\\\"SICA (self-extracted)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"LLM self-extraction\\\\\\\", 79.41, 0.00, 1.0]\\\\n      - [\\\\\\\"Oracle-SICA\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Gold FOL + Z3\\\\\\\", 88.24, \\\\\\\"+8.82\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"6.15e-05\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Key evidence separating extraction quality from aggregation mechanism\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab3_ablation\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Constraint ablation on N=804 problems (Qwen2.5-14B): MAX-SAT vs. count-only vs. random-weight aggregation yield near-identical accuracy (agreement: 802/804).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [Aggregation, \\\\\\\"Accuracy(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"McNemar p vs SC\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: sica_constraint_ablation_013\\\\\\\"\\\\n    baseline_row: \\\\\\\"SC (majority voting)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab4_temperature\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Temperature ablation (Qwen2.5-14B, FOLIO 60): increasing T from 0.3 to 1.0 monotonically increases C0 (30% to 43%) but SICA-SC delta remains exactly 0 with zero discordant pairs.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [Temperature, \\\\\\\"C0(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SC(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SICA(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Delta(pp)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Discordant\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: temperature-ablation-t03, temperature-ablation-t05, sica_d012_14b, temperature-ablation-t10\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"Directly demonstrates diversity is not the bottleneck\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab5_tiebreak\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Tiebreak analysis: SICA resolves SC ties with 80% accuracy vs. 50% random baseline, but ties are too rare (<5% of problems) to affect aggregate accuracy.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Method, \\\\\\\"Tie Accuracy(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Tied Problems(%)\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: sica_expanded_14b\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab6_k_ablation\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"K-sensitivity ablation (Qwen2.5-14B): SICA never outperforms SC across K={6,8,11,12,16,20}.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: ablation\\\\n    columns: [K, \\\\\\\"SC(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"SICA(%)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Delta(pp)\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: sica_k_sensitivity_14b\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab7_overhead\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Computational overhead: SICA adds ~49% wall-clock time over SC, dominated by constraint extraction (47%).\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Stage, \\\\\\\"Time(s)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Fraction(%)\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: exp-009-overhead-analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 38\\\\n  macro_context:\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"LLM symbolic reasoning and constraint-based aggregation\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"Self-consistency and test-time compute scaling\\\\\\\"\\\\n    - \\\\\\\"Oracle/upper-bound experiments in NLP\\\\\\\"\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"self_consistency_and_variants\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"self-consistency chain of thought voting 2023 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"weighted self-consistency confidence LLM\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Wang et al. 2023 (SC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Chen et al. 2024 (USC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Taubenfeld et al. 2025 (confidence SC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Loo et al. 2025 (SC scaling)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"symbolic_reasoning_llm\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"neuro-symbolic reasoning LLM FOL solver 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Logic-LM LINC symbolic solver language model\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Pan et al. 2023 (Logic-LM)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Olausson et al. 2023 (LINC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Xu et al. 2026 (DyLoS)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"FoVer 2025 (TACL)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LogicAgent 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Aristotle 2025 (ACL)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 8\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"test_time_compute_scaling\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"test-time compute scaling LLM 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"reasoning model diversity collapse temperature\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Snell et al. 2025 (ICLR Oral)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"DeepSeek-R1 2025 (Nature)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Diversity-Aware TTS 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"verification_reranking\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"outcome reward model process reward model verification 2023 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Math-Shepherd verification LLM\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Cobbe et al. 2021 (ORM/GSM8K)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Lightman et al. 2023 (PRM)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"constraint_satisfaction_nlp\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"MAX-SAT constraint satisfaction NLP reasoning 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM constraint propagation formal methods\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"SATBench 2025 (EMNLP)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM Meets CP 2025 (IJCAI)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"debate_multi_agent\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"LLM debate multi-agent reasoning aggregation 2023 2024\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Liang et al. 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Du et al. 2023\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"benchmarks_and_datasets\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"FOLIO benchmark logical reasoning 2022\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"ProofWriter dataset deductive 2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"StrategyQA commonsense reasoning\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Han et al. 2022 (FOLIO)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Tafjord et al. 2021 (ProofWriter)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Geva et al. 2021 (StrategyQA)\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Clark et al. 2018 (ARC)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 4\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"negative_results_analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"negative results NLP analysis paper EMNLP 2024 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"when does method fail systematic evaluation LLM\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite: []\\\\n      target_count: 2\\\\n\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"oracle_upper_bound_experiments\\\\\\\"\\\\n      search_queries:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"oracle upper